<title>USA: U.S. Sen. Torricelli gives budget stance Wednesday.</title>
<headline>U.S. Sen. Torricelli gives budget stance Wednesday.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Jersey Sen. Robert Torricelli, one of two pivotal votes on the balanced budget constitutional amendment, will announce his position Wednesday at 3:30 p.m. (2030 GMT), his office said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The Senate is expected to consider his proposed changes to the constitutional amendment later in the week. He has expressed concern that a constitutional amendment should permit the government to set a capital budget and to respond to economic downturns.</p>
</text>
